  "notes": "GAAP audit, FYE 9/30/2022. Governmental lines from the Statement of Revenues, Expenditures, and Changes in Fund Balances, Total Governmental Funds column (p4). Grants (statement and schedules) have no grantor printed: category other, detail_category Grants (the ARP Act Fund shows no grants this year). ending_cash = cash and cash equivalents + cash at county treasurer from the governmental funds Balance Sheet (p3); investments 17,904,767 in ending_investments; beginning cash not printed. Business-type from the proprietary statements, Total Enterprise Funds column (pp5-6); the Governmental Activities Internal Service Fund column is excluded. Business-type receipts total = operating revenues 20,690,341 + investment earnings 231,405 (no single printed total); disbursements = operating expenses 10,239,814 + interest expense, net 985,541 (= Statement of Activities business-type expenses 11,225,355, p2). Proprietary Miscellaneous 307,496 is in Charges for Services on the Statement of Activities (20,658,890 = operating revenues less operating grants), so charges for services. Utility spending by cost type with function utilities. Proprietary cash flows from Total Enterprise Funds (p7). Balance sheet = government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1) by activity column. Detail = the five budget-basis budget-to-actual schedules (General, Streets/Engineering, Sales Tax, 1/2 Cent Sales Tax, ARP Act; pp8-12); zero-actual lines not recorded: General Fund 'Proceeds from issuance of bonds and notes' (budget 5,000,000), Sales Tax Fund 'Other expenses' (-), 1/2 Cent Sales Tax Fund 'Principal' (actual '-', budget 600,000; the GAAP statement p4 shows principal 600,000 in that fund). No schedules for nonmajor or enterprise funds, so no statement lines added for them. Read pages 1-12 of 12"
}
